conjugate-pmns-matrix-element-60b8b37f.interpretation:
The element $U_{\beta i}^*$ is the complex conjugate of the entry located at row $\beta$ (flavor index corresponding to $e, \mu, \tau$) and column $i$ (mass eigenstate index $1, 2, 3$) in the unitary $3 \times 3$ PMNS matrix. In neutrino oscillation probabilities $P(\nu_\alpha \to \nu_\beta)$, interference terms explicitly combine pairs of elements with their complex conjugates as $U_{\alpha i}^* U_{\beta i} U_{\alpha j} U_{\beta j}^*$. For antineutrino oscillations $P(\bar{
u}_\alpha \to \bar{
u}_\beta)$, complex conjugation of the elements replaces $U$ with $U^*$, directly testing leptonic CP invariance.
